<title>UK: RTZ hit by CRA share drop, copper worries.</title>
<headline>RTZ hit by CRA share drop, copper worries.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK metals group RTZ Plc dropped in early dealings on Wednesday, under pressure from a fall in stocks of Australian partner CRA Ltd and worries about RTZ's interim report on Thursday.</p>
<p>RTZ was trading 15p or 1.6 percent lower at 942-1/2p by 0723 GMT while the FTSE 100 index was indicated marginally lower.</p>
<p>CRA shares had dropped amid concerns about profit downgrades after gloomy company forecasts for copper prices.</p>
<p>&quot;CRA weighed on RTZ this morning and there is some nervousness about RTZ's results which are due tomorrow,&quot; said one marketmaker.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542</p>
